    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24745" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δι-ᾰείδω</span></b>  (B), fut.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ᾰείσομαι</span>: 
			Att.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δι-ᾴδω</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ᾴσομαι</span>:—
			Med.
		, aor.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διᾴσασθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phryn.
					<u>PS</u>
					p.65B.
				</span></i>
			:—<i>contend in singing,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινί</span>
			<i>with</i> one, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				5.22
			</span></i>: abs., <i>contend in song, sing for the prize,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Po.</u>
				1462a7
			</span></i>, Phryn.l.c. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>to be dissonant,</i> opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">συνᾴδω,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Heraclit.
				10
			</span></i>.</div>
